
Description:

New jmap_require_accountid option.  When enabled, a JMAP method call that
omits accountId, or gives a null or non-string one, is rejected with
invalidArguments as RFC 8620 requires, instead of being run against the
authenticated user's own account.  Core/echo is the one method that takes
no accountId.  Off by default, so existing clients are unaffected.

Cassandane's JMAP suites run with the option on, and the tester supplies
the user's own accountId on every call.


Documentation:

lib/imapoptions/jmap_require_accountid.  The behaviour follows RFC 8620
Section 3.6.2 as written.


Config changes:

jmap_require_accountid (switch, default off): reject a JMAP method call
that omits accountId, as RFC 8620 requires, rather than defaulting it to
the authenticated user's account.


Upgrade instructions:

None by default.  Before enabling jmap_require_accountid, make sure every
JMAP client sends accountId on every method call, as RFC 8620 has always
required.


